                <pb facs="0047" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v27/pg5"/>

                <head>3. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On July 17–18, 1964, the Australia-New Zealand-United States (ANZUS) Pact held
                    its Council meetings in Washington. Secretary Rusk headed the United States
                    delegation, Prime Minister Keith Holyoake headed the New Zealand delegation, and
                    Foreign Minister Paul Hasluck headed the Australian delegation. Extensive notes
                    of the sessions, prepared <pb facs="0048" n="6" xml:id="pg6"/> on August 20 by
                    the Officer-in-Charge of Australia, New Zealand, and Pacific Affairs Edward J.
                    Thrasher and Thomas F. Conlon of the Office of Southwest Pacific Affairs, are in
                    Department of State, Central Files, DEF 4 ANZUS. Additional documentation on the
                    meeting can be found in Department of State, S/S-Conference Files: Lot 66 D 110,
                    CF 759.</p>
                <p>At the end of the ANZUS meeting, July 18, the Council issued a communiqué which
                    is printed in American Foreign Policy: Current Documents, 1964, pages
                    839–841.</p>
            </div>
